John Campbell wrote:
>
> 	No, autopickup is evil. Turn it off in your .nethackrc.

Autopickup is not evil. It is a great time saver, but it needs to be
used with restraint -- specifically, with a generous dose of
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTIONs. Allow me to offer an excerpt from my defaults.nh
as an example:

OPTIONS=autopickup,pickup_types:$"=/!?+*(
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*rock*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION="<*luckstone*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION="<*touchstone*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*loadstone*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*gray stone*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*flint*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*chest*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*box*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*pick*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">* cursed*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">* worthless*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*==*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION="<*!!*"



